From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ole Algoritme <olealgoritme@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 03:25:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nvk: NVK_PASS_PROFILE=4 method histogram per pass, indirect
 push on again

CS2 on 405.14 (static scene, NVK_PASS_PROFILE=1): the 2x MSAA depth
prepass takes 13 ms for 122 draw calls (119.5 indirect, 368.5 draws),
about 110 us per call, and NVK_INDIRECT_PUSH barely changes it, so the
per-draw record read is not the main cost.  Something recorded between
the calls is.

NVK_PASS_PROFILE=4 (diagnostics only, off by default) counts, per render
pass signature, every method recorded inside the pass: 3D-class methods
by address (MME macro calls by name, and their parameters), writes to
other subchannels as one number.  Each pass line is followed by the 24
most written 3D methods, per recorded pass.  The counts are taken on the
CPU when the pass is recorded, from the pushbuffer itself, so they show
what NVK emitted, including what the MME macros were given, but not the
methods the macros emit on the GPU.  Level 4 also samples the level-2
counters (VS/clipper/PS invocations); the ZCULL counters stay at level 3
only.

NVK_INDIRECT_PUSH is on by default again: 405.14 ran it clean (0 Xid)
with 0032's ring fix, at lower CPU use (0.74-0.94 cores against ~1.6).

No MME macro change: 2160 dwords for a DXVK device, within the 2976
budget checked at queue creation.
